const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文提出自由现金流、公司融资和控制权交易中的代理冲突问题。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1818789",label:{zh:"The American Economic Review (1986) · 来源说明",en:"The American Economic Review (1986) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源以公司控制、现金流配置和管理者激励的理论讨论组织，而不是一套直接可运行的评分模型。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1818789",label:{zh:"The American Economic Review (1986) · 来源说明",en:"The American Economic Review (1986) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"若进行经验延伸，需要现金流、投资、分配、收购记录、治理结构与各项信息的披露时点。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1818789",label:{zh:"The American Economic Review (1986) · 来源说明",en:"The American Economic Review (1986) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"概念框架帮助区分现金流配置与控制权激励，但不将高现金或某类交易自动标记为低效。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1818789",label:{zh:"The American Economic Review (1986) · 来源说明",en:"The American Economic Review (1986) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"明确自由现金流定义、企业生命周期、资本支出和分配口径，保留治理与交易文件版本，并区分公告与完成日期。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1818789",label:{zh:"The American Economic Review (1986) · 来源说明",en:"The American Economic Review (1986) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The American Economic Review (1986)。理论机制不能独自裁定某项收购或资本配置的质量，也不构成估值、公司行动或投资建议。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The American Economic Review (1986) for “Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1818789",label:{zh:"The American Economic Review (1986) · 来源说明",en:"The American Economic Review (1986) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。理论机制不能独自裁定某项收购或资本配置的质量，也不构成估值、公司行动或投资建议。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Agency Costs of Free Cash Flow, Corporate Finance, and Takeovers”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
